//@ run-pass
//@ expect-stdout: before
//@ expect-stdout: after
//@ description: `println()` prints an empty line on both engines. lean_single printed `0` because the `)` fell to compile_primary's last arm. The substring checks above cannot see a stray `0`; scripts/ci/engine_parity_gate.sh compares the two engines' full stdout and does.

fn main() with IO {
    println("before")
    println()
    println("after")
}
